# Git: new branch per work session

When starting a new task or continuing after a completed PR/commit wave:

- **Create a new branch first** — do not keep committing on the previous feature branch.
- Name branches by intent, e.g. `fix/…`, `feat/…`, `chore/…`.
- Base the branch on the appropriate upstream (`dev`, `main`, or the open cutover branch only when stacking intentionally).
- Commit only when asked (or when the user explicitly requests push/PR); then **push the new branch** and **open a new PR**.
- Prefer a focused PR for the current change set; do not dump unrelated work onto an old branch.

## Examples

```bash
# ✅ Start fresh
git checkout dev   # or the agreed base
git pull
git checkout -b fix/creators-footer-onboarding-exit

# ❌ Continue piling onto the last branch
git checkout feat/convex-cutover-stripe
git commit ...
```

Stack onto an existing feature branch only when the user asks for a stacked PR or the change depends on unmerged work on that branch.
